alk but not sing."},{"mode":"walking","label":"Brisk or incline walking","minutes":40,"intensity":"moderate","exerciseId":"startfit:brisk-walking","weekday":2,"note":"Moderate effort: you can talk but not sing."},{"mode":"walking","label":"Brisk or incline walking","minutes":40,"intensity":"moderate","exerciseId":"startfit:brisk-walking","weekday":5,"note":"Moderate effort: you can talk but not sing."},{"mode":"walking","label":"Brisk or incline walking","minutes":40,"intensity":"moderate","exerciseId":"startfit:brisk-walking","weekday":6,"note":"Moderate effort: you can talk but not sing."}],"cardioMinutesPerWeek":185,"cardioTargetMinutes":200,"cardioRamp":[200,200,200,200,200,200],"notes":[{"kind":"adjustment","text":"Chest is below the weekly target because the sessions are full. More minutes per session or another training day would close the gap."}],"claimIds":["acsm_days","vol_fractional","vol_dose","vol_session_cap","vol_targets_design","exercise_order","warmup","load_range","failure_optional","failure_proximity","rir_scale","rest_hypertrophy","freq_hypertrophy","progress_both","progress_increase","deload_concept","deload_rule","who_activity","hiit_time","concurrent","rt_body_fat"],"rationale":[{"claimId":"acsm_days","decision":"4 strength days a week, matching the time you have."},{"claimId":"vol_fractional","decision":"Weekly sets are counted as 1 for the main muscle and ½ for helping muscles, and each muscle group gets a target range."},{"claimId":"vol_dose","decision":"Targets for your level are 10–16 weekly sets for the big muscle groups (fewer for calves and abs)."},{"claimId":"exercise_order","decision":"Each session starts with the big multi-joint lifts and ends with smaller single-joint and core exercises."},{"claimId":"warmup","decision":"Every session starts with a short general warm-up and lighter practice sets."},{"claimId":"load_range","decision":"Main lifts use 6–10 repetitions and smaller exercises use higher repetitions; lighter and heavier loads both build muscle."},{"claimId":"failure_optional","decision":"Sets stop about 2 repetitions short of failure on the main lifts; training to failure is not required."},{"claimId":"failure_proximity","decision":"Smaller exercises go a little closer to failure (about 1–2 repetitions in reserve) because growth tends to improve closer to failure."},{"claimId":"rest_hypertrophy","decision":"Rest about 2.5 minutes after main-lift sets and 75 seconds after smaller exercises."},{"claimId":"freq_hypertrophy","decision":"Each major muscle group is trained on at least two days, spreading the weekly sets so each session stays manageable."},{"claimId":"progress_both","decision":"Progress by adding repetitions first, then weight (double progression)."},{"claimId":"progress_increase","decision":"Load increases of about 2–10% once you can do 1–2 repetitions more than planned."},{"claimId":"deload_concept","decision":"A lighter week is planned as an option, used when tiredness or performance call for it."},{"claimId":"who_activity","decision":"200 minutes of cardio a week, inside the WHO range of 150–300."},{"claimId":"hiit_time","decision":"One session a week is intervals, which saves time for similar body-composition results."},{"claimId":"concurrent","decision":"Cardio goes on other days or at least a few hours away from lifting where possible, so it does not blunt your strength sessions."},{"claimId":"rt_body_fat","decision":"Strength training stays the core of the plan while you lose fat."}],"inputs":{"goal":"fat_loss","experience":"intermediate","daysPerWeek":4,"sessionMinutes":60,"equipment":["bodyweight","dumbbell","barbell","ez_bar","rack","bench","kettlebell","cable","machine","smith_machine","band","pullup_bar","dip_bars","trap_bar","landmine","medicine_ball","exercise_ball","foam_roller","ab_wheel","box","rings","suspension","sled","strongman","cardio_machine","other"],"age":30,"pain":[],"priorityMuscles":[],"currentActivity":"regular","screeningStatus":"ok"}}'::jso