"Load increases of about 2–10% once you can do 1–2 repetitions more than planned."},{"claimId":"deload_concept","decision":"A lighter week is planned as an option, used when tiredness or performance call for it."},{"claimId":"who_activity","decision":"150 minutes of cardio a week, inside the WHO range of 150–300."},{"claimId":"concurrent","decision":"Cardio goes on other days or at least a few hours away from lifting where possible, so it does not blunt your strength sessions."},{"claimId":"injury_prevention","decision":"Strength work is kept in every week; it was linked to fewer sports injuries, stretching alone was not."}],"inputs":{"goal":"general","experience":"beginner","daysPerWeek":3,"sessionMinutes":45,"equipment":["bodyweight","dumbbell","barbell","ez_bar","rack","bench","kettlebell","cable","machine","smith_machine","band","pullup_bar","dip_bars","trap_bar","landmine","medicine_ball","exercise_ball","foam_roller","ab_wheel","box","rings","suspension","sled","strongman","cardio_machine","other"],"age":30,"pain":[],"priorityMuscles":[],"currentActivity":"regular","screeningStatus":"ok"}}'::jsonb, 'library')
