because your goal is endurance."},{"claimId":"vol_fractional","decision":"Weekly sets are counted as 1 for the main muscle and ½ for helping muscles, and each muscle group gets a target range."},{"claimId":"vol_minimum","decision":"Targets start at about 4 weekly sets per muscle group, the time-efficient minimum, and go higher when time allows."},{"claimId":"exercise_order","decision":"Each session starts with the big multi-joint lifts and ends with smaller single-joint and core exercises."},{"claimId":"warmup","decision":"Every session starts with a short general warm-up and lighter practice sets."},{"claimId":"load_range","decision":"Main lifts use 10–15 repetitions and smaller exercises use higher repetitions; lighter and heavier loads both build muscle."},{"claimId":"failure_optional","decision":"Sets stop about 3 repetitions short of failure on the main lifts; training to failure is not required."},{"claimId":"failure_proximity","decision":"Smaller exercises go a little closer to failure (about 1–2 repetitions in reserve) because growth tends to improve closer to failure."},{"claimId":"rest_intervals","decision":"Rest about 2 minutes after main-lift sets and 75 seconds after smaller exercises."},{"claimId":"freq_hypertrophy","decision":"Each major muscle group is trained on at least two days, spreading the weekly sets so each session stays manageable."},{"claimId":"progress_both","decision":"Progress by adding repetitions first, then weight (double progression)."},{"claimId":"progress_increase","decision":"Load increases of about 2–10% once you can do 1–2 repetitions more than planned."},{"claimId":"deload_concept","decision":"A lighter week is planned as an option, used when tiredness or performance call for it."},{"claimId":"who_activity","decision":"240 minutes of cardio a week, inside the WHO range of 150–300."},{"claimId":"hiit_time","decision":"One session a week is intervals, which saves time for similar body-composition results."},{"claimId":"concurrent","decision":"Cardio goes on other days or at least a few hours away from lifting where possible, so it does not blunt your strength sessions."},{"claimId":"injury_prevention","decision":"Strength work is kept in every week; it was linked to fewer sports injuries, stretching alone was not."}],"inputs":{"goal":"endurance","experience":"beginner","daysPerWeek":4,"sessionMinutes":45,"equipment":["bodyweight","dumbbell","barbell","ez_bar","rack","bench","kettlebell","cable","machine","smith_machine","band","pullup_bar","dip_bars","trap_bar","landmine","medicine_ball","exercise_ball","foam_roller","ab_wheel","box","rings","suspension","sled","strongman","cardio_machine","other"],"age":30,"pain":[],"priorityMuscles":[],"currentActivity":"regular","screeningStatus":"ok"}}'::jsonb, 'library')
